# Example: Dispatch Agent Scope Rules for CLAUDE.md

Add this section to your project's CLAUDE.md file. Adjust the paths
to match your project structure.

---

## Dispatch Agent Scope

When running as the Dispatch automated agent (issues labelled `dispatch`):

### Allowed
- Create/edit files in: `src/app/`, `src/components/`, `src/hooks/`
- Add new UI components following existing patterns
- Add columns, filters, sorting, search to existing tables and displays
- Add CSV/PDF/JSON export features that read from existing API routes
- Create new read-only API routes (GET only) in `src/app/api/`
- Modify styles, layouts, pages, loading states, empty states

### Forbidden
- `src/lib/auth/` — authentication logic
- `src/lib/db/` — database schema and migrations
- `src/lib/api/` — core API integrations
- `.env`, `.env.example` — environment variables
- `package.json` — do not add or remove dependencies
- `scripts/` — operational and deployment scripts
- Any API route that writes to the database (POST/PATCH/DELETE)

### Verification
Run all before opening a PR:
- `npm run build`
- `npm run lint`
- `npm run typecheck`
